diff --git a/docs/api_to_audit.md b/docs/api_to_audit.md
index 7746895..4eefb8c 100644
--- a/docs/api_to_audit.md
+++ b/docs/api_to_audit.md
@@ -5008,3 +5008,49 @@ precedence, bounded discovery failure, and module-ABI preservation after Node
 replacement. Settle the shared process-local instance lifecycle across SDK
 bundle versions and whether `bundledNpmCli` belongs on the public surface before
 removing the prefix.
+
+## Native effective execution policies
+
+`bb.experimental_executionPolicies` is a provider-scoped, plugin-attributed native service.
+`register` accepts only model, reasoning level and service tier. Core shares this
+implementation for event provenance, option mutation guards, dispatch admission,
+last-execution restoration and the final synchronous host send. It never grants
+a plugin permission to alter the provider, input, source, history or permissions.
+Registration is staged until atomic plugin activation. A replacement lease takes
+over from the same owner without letting the old lease disable it. Release stops
+new overlays, while durable original-execution readers remain in core. A process
+restart resumes an enabled policy only when its owner registers again; absent
+owners leave source restoration active and effective overlays disabled.
+
+Protocol `bb.execution-policy/v1` describes the required semantic identifiers.
+`catalog-profile-validation` confirms that native host catalogs validate reasoning
+and service tiers. Models without reasoning choices accept only their known
+catalog default; unknown discovery and unsupported tiers remain unavailable.
+Final transport omits reasoning that the target model does not support, using
+the same native catalog rule for effective and restored execution. Raw original
+profiles and provider-specific options remain unchanged.
+`consistent-durable-registry` confirms that startup validates the complete policy
+registry against its journal inventory before loading any registration. Missing,
+empty or partial registries with surviving journals block registration, dispatch
+and provenance reads until operator recovery. An absent or empty policy directory
+remains a supported first installation and is not written during startup.
+All public status and refusal messages use English. The Plugin Guide lists the
+SDK symbols under Effective execution policies. Every native send uses the same
+final boundary; message.dispatch remains proceed/wait/reject only.
+
+Before stabilization, audit multi-host provider continuation, crash/restart and
+uninstall restoration, journal corruption, immutable null/Fast profiles, native
+catalog cancellation and cooldown, concurrent plugin reloads, provenance retention,
+and target-host changes after preparation. Companion session handshakes require
+`executionPolicyProtocol=bb.execution-policy/v1` as well as protocol 273. This
+prevents stock daemons with a matching numeric version from being admitted.
+
+Policy activation waits on the native provider registry when factories load
+in a different startup order. Pending controllers remain unavailable until
+the provider registers; unknown providers never gain execution authority.
+The wait is bounded and aborted on release. Completing registration notifies
+the owner immediately so clients do not need a reload or execution polling.
+
+The server-owned `execution-policies/` tree participates in native server
+archives and imports, so moving a server retains selection and request restore
+provenance even if the originating plugin is later removed.
